# The review of the first pull request: apply's all or none.

[break] apply-an-unreadable-file-is-taken-as-absent
rule: A file that is there and cannot be read is an error that writes nothing, never "not there", which putting back would delete.
file: xtask/src/apply.rs
in: run_with
find: Err(error) if error.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => Ok((None, None)),
replace: Err(_) => Ok((None, None)),
caught-by:
    apply::tests::a_file_that_is_there_and_cannot_be_read_is_never_taken_as_absent

[break] apply-one-file-spelt-two-ways-is-two
rule: One file spelt two ways is one file of the plan, so neither change is lost.
file: xtask/src/apply.rs
